The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
cfg.setProperty(Property.TSERV_NATIVEMAP_ENABLED, Boolean.TRUE.toString());
```
Reason:
The `setProperty` call for enabling the native map functionality was executed without ensuring that the native library was available. This led to the `testExistingInstance` test failing when the native path was not set correctly in `MiniAccumuloConfigImpl.useExistingInstance`, as the check for the presence of the native library was enforced after changes made in ACCUMULO-4596.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
// The line that was removed to prevent enabling the native map when the library is not available
// cfg.setProperty(Property.TSERV_NATIVEMAP_ENABLED, Boolean.TRUE.toString());
```
Reason:
By removing the line that enables the native map functionality, the code prevents the test from failing when the native library is not available. This ensures that the test can run successfully without relying on the native library, thus addressing the root cause of the failure in the `testExistingInstance` test.

